Hi Matt,

Thanks for providing an example.  After spending a couple hours going
back and forth between facet wrap and facet grid, I came up with two
things:

1) I think whatever happens happens at build_strip, panel_info, or
layout_grid, maybe with one of these two lines:
row_vars <- unique(.$panel_info[names(.$rows)])
labels[, i] <- labeller(names(label_df)[i], label_df[, i])
But, I do not understand the guts of ggplot2 (/proto?) to be able to
properly debug so I could watch what is happening.

2) It is not on the rows, but you can get a column label using:
ggplot(df.single, aes(x, y)) + geom_line() + facet_wrap(~ a)

HTH,

Josh

P. S. I was also re-impressed with the sheer amount of work and
careful attention to detail Hadley must have put forth to make all of
this.  Wow, and thanks.

