Manuel,

> How can I get the x and y from the shapefile?  I think the x and y are in the shp file (within the shapefile), right? but how can I use geom_path to get this information?

you will have to have a closer look at the object that you get from reading the shapefile, but usually there will be a slot called "polygons" or "lines" that will give you the x and y information. Something along the lines:

xx <- read.shapefile(...)
slots(xx[[1]] ,"lines")
slots(xx[[1]] ,"polygons")

Heike

