The agricolae package has many other methods of mean separation built-in if you don't want LSD. You can also use ldply to see if the output of another package's mean test will give you the abcdefghijk that you want. If it doesn't you can always take a look at the code and tweak it to output the letters or p-values or whatever you want.

If you play with it and get it looking/working awesomer let me know cause it's something I may revisit in the near future.

B

