> I read the table as data.frame name "all" and want to plot it in a bar chart
> with two facets - "Score" and "Type", and a group comparing means of
> different "Number" value side by side. I also want to show the error bars of
> standard deviation. I use the following code to plot:
>
> a <- qplot(Methods, Mean, fill = Number, data = all, geom = "bar", position
> = "dodge") + geom_errorbar(aes(ymax = Score + Error, ymin = Score - Error),
> position = "dodge") + facet_grid(Score ~ Type) + theme_bw()
> print(a)
>
> But I met the error:
> Error in get("transform", env = ., inherits = TRUE)(., ...) :
>   attempt to apply non-function
> Calls: print ... <Anonymous> -> <Anonymous> -> <Anonymous> -> <Anonymous>
> Execution halted
>
> Does anyone can help me on this? Thanks a lot!

I got an error with your code, but not the same one you got.  In your
code, the call to geom_errorbar doesn't make sense.  Score is a factor
(and so doesn't make sense being plotted on the scale that was created
by Mean) and Error is not defined in your data.  The following did
work for me:

qplot(Methods, Mean, fill = factor(Number),

	data = all, geom = "bar", position = "dodge") +

	geom_errorbar(aes(ymax = Mean + SD, ymin = Mean - SD),

		position = "dodge") +
	facet_grid(Score ~ Type) + theme_bw()

Number must be a factor in your data.frame; maybe it was in yours, but
that isn't clear how you presented the data.

Finally, I'm under obligation to make the warning to not make a
"dynamite plot":

http://biostat.mc.vanderbilt.edu/wiki/Main/DynamitePlots

http://biostat.mc.vanderbilt.edu/twiki/pub/Main/TatsukiRcode/Poster3.pdf

> --
> Best,
> Zhenjiang

