ok, it gets uglier, but it works
In each aes, after colour, add "alpha=0" if you want the line "gone"

e.g.
geom_line(data=d.p[which(d.p$I==-1),],aes(x=K, y=err, group=I, colour=ordered(I),alpha=0))

then you'll get an alpha legend you dont want, so

+scale_alpha(legend=FALSE)

at the end of the ggplot() command.

still not attractive.

On Mon, Nov 29, 2010 at 10:31 PM, James McCreight <mccr...@colorado.edu> wrote:
> ah, i retract that solution. as you take out more colors, the pallette starts changing. it was hardly noticable when removing just one color. sorry to speak too soon.
